        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What is included in the Morocco Film Location and Heritage Cinema tour?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "This comprehensive 1-day private excursion includes round-trip private transport from your Marrakech hotel or riad in a premium air-conditioned 4x4 or Mercedes minivan, an experienced English-speaking Moroccan chauffeur, crossing the High Atlas via Tizi n'Tichka Pass (2,260m), an official walking tour of UNESCO Ksar Ait Benhaddou, and admission to Atlas Film Studios and CLA Studios in Ouarzazate."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Can visitors walk inside Atlas Film Studios in Ouarzazate?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Yes. Atlas Film Studios (spanning over 300,000 square meters) offers guided access to preserved movie sets, including ancient Egyptian temples, Roman amphitheaters, Tibetan monasteries, and medieval biblical fortresses. You can walk through the set architecture and explore behind-the-scenes production workshops."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How long is the drive from Marrakech to Ait Benhaddou and Ouarzazate?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "The scenic drive from Marrakech to Ait Benhaddou takes approximately 3.5 to 4 hours each way, winding through the High Atlas Mountains. We depart early (around 07:30 AM) to maximize sightseeing time, with scenic rest pauses along the Tizi n'Tichka pass. The full-day excursion spans 11 to 12 hours total."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Can this film location tour be customized or extended to the Sahara Desert?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Yes, absolutely. Because all Roam Morocco journeys are 100% private, you can seamlessly extend this single-day cinema itinerary into a 3-day or 4-day desert expedition through Dades Gorge and Todra Valley to the Erg Chebbi luxury dunes in Merzouga, finishing either back in Marrakech or onward in Fes."
        }
      }
    ]
  }
];
---
<Layout lang="it" title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} ogImage={ogImage} bodyClass={bodyClass} extraStyles={extraStyles} schema={schema}>
  <style is:inline slot="head">

    :root {
      --bg-cream: #f2eee6;
      --card-bg: #ffffff;
      --border-subtle: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12);
      --border-strong: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.22);
      --text-main: #000000;
      --text-muted: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.72);
      --red: #f10b18;
    }

    *, *::before, *::after {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    html, body {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      font-family: 'Inter', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      background: #f2eee6 !important;
      color: #000000 !important;
      overflow-x: hidden;
      -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
    }

    main.roam-tour-main {
      background: #f2eee6 !important;
      color: #000000 !important;
      padding: 120px 24px 80px !important;
    }

    .roam-tour-wrapper {
      max-width: 960px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .roam-tour-badge {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 8px;
      font-family: 'Inter', -apple-system, sans-serif;
      font-size: 11px;
      font-weight: 700;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: .08em;
      color: #8A6A23;
      background: rgba(200, 164, 92, 0.12);
      border: 1px solid rgba(200, 164, 92, 0.28);
      padding: 6px 14px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      margin-bottom: 20px;
    }
    .roam-tour-badge::before {
      content: "";
      width: 6px;
      height: 6px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: #C8A45C;
    }

    .roam-tour-title {
      font-family: 'Inter', -apple-system, sans-serif !important;
      font-size: clamp(34px, 5.5vw, 62px) !important;
      font-weight: 800 !important;
      letter-spacing: -.04em !important;
      line-height: 1.05 !important;
      text-transform: uppercase !important;
      color: #000000 !important;
      margin: 0 0 20px !important;
    }

